blocks.md:
For a web app the surface includes more than the pages you designed:

- every route and API method, especially those that need no login;
- every open network port and the services behind them;
- file uploads, webhooks (URLs that other services call), and admin consoles;
- the libraries and services you depend on;
- people and partners with access, such as support staff and vendor accounts.

The DFD from the last lesson helps: every entry point on a flow that crosses a trust boundary is part of the surface. Smaller surface, fewer places to defend.

